(window.LADDER_CARDS["16·logi"]=window.LADDER_CARDS["16·logi"]||[]).push(
 {"u":"16·logi.1.1","q":"What does the tank-level technique say, and how do the model day's books close?","a":"V(T) = V(0) + ∫₀ᵀ (in − out): the water now is the start plus the area under in less out; over the day the area is 0, since the pump puts back the 2112 m³ drawn","w":["V(T) = ∫₀ᵀ in, whatever is drawn; over the day the tank gains 2112 m³","V(T) = V(0) + in(T) − out(T); over the day the tank loses 24 m³","V(T) = V(0) − ∫₀ᵀ (in − out); over the day the area is 110.9 m³"],"why":"It is net-change with Q = V. The pump's 88 m³/h is the day's average outflow, so ∫₀²⁴ (in − out) = 0."},
 {"u":"16·logi.2.1","q":"When is the tank lowest, and why not at noon?","a":"at about 18.93 h, near 6:56 in the evening, when the draw falls back to the pump's rate; at noon the town draws hardest but the tank is still well up","w":["at noon, when the town draws hardest","at about 5.07 h, when the draw first passes the pump's rate","at midnight, when the day's whole draw is gone"],"why":"in − out is − between 5.07 and 18.93, so the level falls all that time. It is 110.9 m³ below the start at the trough."},
 {"u":"16·logi.3.1","q":"What does never-dry say, and how big must the tank be?","a":"a tank never runs dry exactly when it starts with at least its deepest dip, 110.9 m³ here; with the swing from crest to trough and water kept back for fires, it needs about 902 m³","w":["a tank never runs dry when it starts full; it needs the day's 2112 m³","a tank never runs dry when the pump runs at the average rate; it needs 110.9 m³ in all","a tank never runs dry exactly when it starts with its morning crest; it needs 680 m³"],"why":"V(t) = V(0) − G(t), and G reaches a greatest value D by highest-and-lowest. The 902 is 680 for fires plus the swing of 221.7."},
 {"u":"16·logi.4.1","q":"What does pump-rate say, and why does no start save a slow pump?","a":"a pump slower than the average outflow runs any tank dry in the end; at 87 m³/h the tank loses 24 m³ every day, so after n days it is down 24n from any start","w":["a pump slower than the greatest outflow runs the tank dry in a day; a bigger start saves it","a pump at any rate keeps the tank safe if it starts full","a pump faster than the average outflow runs the tank dry; no start saves it"],"why":"Over a day the level changes by 24(r − 88). A fixed loss a day passes any fixed start."},
 {"u":"16·logi.5.1","q":"Why is “start with the day's whole draw, to be safe” a move to watch out for?","a":"the deepest dip is enough, 110.9 m³ and not 2112, since the pump is putting water back all day","w":["the day's whole draw is too little: the tank needs twice it","no start is safe, whatever the pump does","the start does not matter at all"],"why":"Never-dry asks only for the greatest value of ∫₀ᵗ (out − in). The draw counts only against what has come in."});
/* end phase F und_r16 */
